  "notable_quotes": [
    "Immobilizing H2O in TYUT-ATZ as CO2 binding sites is proposed to suppress H2O/CO2 competition during humid-gas separation.",
    "SC-XRD, FT-IR, and DFT indicate pore-confined H2O is uniformly distributed and hydrogen-bonds to CO2 adsorbed in side pockets.",
    "TYUT-ATZ-β has the highest CO2/H2O uptake ratio in humid flue gas, attributed to excellent water stability and unique H2O sites."
